F1: disable swap, or use plain dm-crypt swap with a fresh random key at each boot (/etc/crypttab: NAME DEVICE /dev/urandom plain,swap,cipher=aes-xts-plain64,size=256); activate only that mapped swap device and reboot to verify the boot configuration.
F2: disable host crash reporters (including apport and systemd-coredump); persist kernel.core_pattern= and kernel.core_uses_pid=0 in /etc/sysctl.d/99-no-core.conf, apply those settings and verify they remain after reboot.
